WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:05.939
This lesson shows you how to create a new event or update an existing event on the live website.

2
00:00:05.939 --> 00:00:16.611
We will work as a draft, enter every required detail, preview the result, save it safely, clear the applicable cache, and verify what visitors can see on the public Events page.

3
00:00:16.961 --> 00:00:23.677
You need a WordPress account with the Editor or Administrator role. Editor access is enough for this task.

4
00:00:23.677 --> 00:00:29.316
If Events is missing from the left menu, stop and ask the website administrator for help.

5
00:00:29.316 --> 00:00:33.688
This lesson does not create users, change roles, or manage passwords.

6
00:00:34.038 --> 00:00:39.572
Open a web browser and go to rebekahspureliving.com forward slash W P dash admin.

7
00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:43.466
Enter your own username and password, then select Log In.

8
00:00:43.466 --> 00:00:50.434
Confirm that the address is the live rebekahspureliving.com domain. Do not use an old staging address.

9
00:00:50.784 --> 00:00:56.703
In the black menu on the left, select Events. To create a new event, select Add New Event.

10
00:00:56.703 --> 00:01:02.293
To update an event, stay on the Events list, find the correct title, and select Edit.

11
00:01:02.293 --> 00:01:07.160
Always confirm that you opened the correct event before changing anything.

12
00:01:07.510 --> 00:01:10.547
For a new event, enter the exact approved title.

13
00:01:10.547 --> 00:01:19.721
In the main Visual editor, enter the complete public description, including what the event is, who it is for, and any instructions visitors need.

14
00:01:19.721 --> 00:01:25.731
Select Save Draft while you work. Do not publish an event that is missing required information.

15
00:01:26.081 --> 00:01:33.653
In Event Categories, check the store location connected to the event: Clarkston, Grand Blanc, Lake Orion, or Lapeer.

16
00:01:33.653 --> 00:01:38.352
Choose only the correct location. Do not create a new category or guess.

17
00:01:38.352 --> 00:01:43.117
The category helps visitors find events for the store they plan to visit.

18
00:01:43.467 --> 00:01:50.502
Enter the start date, start time, end date, and end time. Use All Day only when it is truly an all-day event.

19
00:01:50.502 --> 00:01:56.827
Confirm the America slash Detroit time zone. Choose an existing venue and organizer when possible.

20
00:01:56.827 --> 00:02:03.668
Add the cost, external event website if needed, and a sixteen-by-nine featured image with useful alt text.

21
00:02:04.018 --> 00:02:07.752
Select Preview and inspect the event before publishing.

22
00:02:07.752 --> 00:02:13.928
Confirm the title, description, store, date, time, venue, organizer, cost, link, and image.

23
00:02:13.928 --> 00:02:16.915
Check the preview at desktop and phone size.

24
00:02:16.915 --> 00:02:23.635
If anything is wrong or uncertain, return to the editor, correct it, and keep the event as a draft.

25
00:02:23.985 --> 00:02:29.717
When a new event is complete and approved, select Publish one time and wait for confirmation.

26
00:02:29.717 --> 00:02:32.553
For an existing event, select Update one time.

27
00:02:32.553 --> 00:02:40.566
If an announced event is canceled, set Events Status to Canceled, add a clear cancellation note to the description, and update it.

28
00:02:40.566 --> 00:02:43.340
Do not immediately delete an announced event.

29
00:02:43.690 --> 00:02:48.104
After saving, return to the Events list. Find the event you changed.

30
00:02:48.104 --> 00:02:52.647
Clear the applicable page or record cache if that option is available.

31
00:02:52.647 --> 00:02:58.877
If the site provides an approved Breeze or Varnish purge control, use only the applicable purge.

32
00:02:58.877 --> 00:03:03.031
Do not change unrelated cache, server, or optimization settings.

33
00:03:03.381 --> 00:03:09.937
Open rebekahspureliving.com forward slash events forward slash without adding anything to the address.

34
00:03:09.937 --> 00:03:13.729
Find the event using the location filter or the event list.

35
00:03:13.729 --> 00:03:19.063
Confirm that the title, date, time, store, image, and link are visible and correct.

36
00:03:19.063 --> 00:03:22.212
Open the event itself and test every public link.

37
00:03:22.562 --> 00:03:25.375
Repeat the public check at a phone-size screen.

38
00:03:25.375 --> 00:03:32.795
Make sure the location filter opens, the event card fits the screen, the text is readable, and no content runs off the side.

39
00:03:32.795 --> 00:03:38.959
A successful WordPress save does not prove that a visitor can see or use the event on the live website.

40
00:03:39.309 --> 00:03:45.339
Every event change ends with the same three checks. First, save or update the correct event.

41
00:03:45.339 --> 00:03:52.877
Second, clear only the applicable cache. Third, verify the exact public event and Events page on desktop and phone.

42
00:03:52.877 --> 00:03:59.104
If the live result is wrong or missing, stop and ask for help instead of making random changes.
